<title>ITALY: Parmalat firmer in Milan on CSFB &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Parmalat firmer in Milan on CSFB &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian food group Parmalat was firmer on the Milan bourse after CSFB initiated coverage of the group with a buy rating with a target price of 3,200 lire.</p>
<p>At 1225 GMT, Parmalat Finanziaria SpA stock was up 3.28 percent at 2,585 lire after a high at 2,610.</p>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston analyst Anne Alexander said Parmalat had a good geographic spread and growth prospects were positive.</p>
<p>She estimated earnings per share of 170 lire this year and 191 lire in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
